	echo "		<limit>: must be in the following format: <size>/<days>"
	echo "		Each table that has more than <size> Gb is splitted in partitions. Split rule: if such table has an indexed timestamp column, each partition will have <days> days. If not, each partition wil have <size> Gb."
	echo "		Size is calculated from table statistics (average row length)."
	echo "			<size>: Min: 1. Max: 999.999"
	echo "			<days>: Min: 1. Max: 100"
	echo "      If environment variable MY_MIRROR_TXN_LEN_FORCE_LIMIT is set, for tables partitioned by PK, each partition will have no more than <MY_MIRROR_TXN_LEN_FORCE_LIMIT> rows, even if average row length is very small."
